+Hello—my 67-year-old father has had trouble falling asleep and waking during the night for about three months. He takes apixaban 5 mg twice daily for atrial fibrillation and has not started a new sleep aid.
+
+Could we assess possible causes and whether CBT-I would be appropriate and accessible? If melatonin comes up, how should his age, apixaban, other medicines, and supplement quality affect the decision? Should he avoid diphenhydramine, doxylamine, or combination nighttime products because of sedation and anticholinergic effects?
+
+We will not start, stop, or change any medicine or dose without clinical guidance. Would a sleep diary or screening for sleep apnea or restless legs help before the visit?
